  "goodToKnow": "Geltend means valid, applicable or current: das geltende Recht (the law in force), die geltenden Regeln. It's the present participle of gelten (to be valid, to count). The key phrase is etwas geltend machen: to assert or claim something, as in Ansprüche geltend machen, Kosten steuerlich geltend machen (to claim costs for tax), a phrase on every German tax form. Sich geltend machen means to make itself felt."
